-- V90: Backfill verified "Merkez"-pattern neighborhoods for the European side (Avrupa yakasi).
-- Sibling of V88 (same pattern, anatolian side) -- see that migration's header for the full
-- methodology explanation. Summary: scripts/audit_european_geodata.py + the 25-district
-- building import (2026-08-14/15) found these neighborhoods referenced by OSM-tagged buildings
-- but with either NO db row or a truncated/non-canonical name -> buildings were skipped at
-- import time (never inserted). Each entry below was independently confirmed BOTH ways before
-- being included: (a) a fresh OSM Overpass fetch resolves a real admin boundary today, cross-
-- checked to have a substantial (>10%) overlap fraction with its claimed district -- a first
-- pass wrongly matched Bagcilar/Gaziosmanpasa "Merkez" queries to a same-named NEIGHBORING
-- district's relation (Gungoren's), caught because the wrong match's district-clipped area was
-- ~0 (a boundary-line graze, not real overlap) -- fixed by scoring every same-named OSM candidate
-- by clipped-area instead of taking the first Overpass result; (b) independent, non-OSM
-- confirmation via Turkey's official TUIK/Icisleri Bakanligi neighborhood list
-- (github.com/bertugfahriozer/il_ilce_mahalle) that this is a real, currently-registered mahalle.
--
-- NOT backfilled (found in the same investigation, deliberately excluded, same precedent as V88's
-- ~50 untouched duplicate-name rows): Eyupsultan's second unmatched name "Merkez" (distinct from
-- "Goktuerk Merkez" below -- not present in the official list under Eyupsultan) and Kagithane's
-- "Emniyetevleri" (also not in the official list -- likely an informal/historic area name, not a
-- current mahalle). Both left as skipped-at-import, documented, not guessed at.

BEGIN;

